THE MAKERS' EFFICIENCY CURVES AT THEIR NEAREST PRINTED POINTS (curve_readings.py, stream l3plane, MESHSAT-1357).
Every figure INFERRED: a pixel reading of a TYPICAL curve (TA 25 C) of the maker's own demonstration circuit, not a
figure for board E or board A. Nothing is measured.

1. LM5176 (board A's front end, U2): TI SNVSAI1D v2/vendor/ti/lm5176-datasheet.pdf sha256/16 98191bec36d43771, p.9 Figure 6-2 'Efficiency vs Load',
   VOUT 12 V, fsw 300 kHz, L1 4.7 uH, the VIN = 9 V curve: a boost at a ratio of 1.33 (board A: 15.1 V to 20 V, 1.32).
   2.5 A 98.0 %; 3.5 A 98.1 %; 4.5 A 98.0 %; 5.5 A 97.9 %; 5.9 A 97.8 %
   READING at 5.5 to 6 A (board A's front end carries U3's 6.1 A): 97.8 to 97.9 % (INFERRED). Board A differs: 20 V out,
   about 200 kHz, 10 uH, CSD19532Q5B. The plot's load current is its OUTPUT current: at 6 A out its 9 V curve draws about
   8.2 A in (12 V x 6 A / 0.978 / 9 V), close to board A's 8.7 A in at 6.1 A out (6.1 A x 20 V / 0.93 / 15.1 V): the
   currents are alike, the voltages and the circuit are not (second issue: CHECK-2 minor 6 corrected this sentence).

2. LT8705A (board E's tracker stage, U5): ADI 8705af v2/vendor/power/lt8705a.pdf sha256/16 8f552a0b57677bfa, p.41 '12V, 15A Output Converter Accepts
   7.5V to 55V Input', 'Efficiency vs Output Current'. Its buck switches M1 and M2 ARE board E's Q3 BSC028N06NS and Q4 BSC039N06NS as
   generated (NETLIST v2/ecad/pcb-e1-dock-e7/out/pcb-e1-dock.net; ARRAY.md section 6's draft moves both to an 80 or 100 V part for the 2S2P array):
   VIN 35 V (a buck, 35 to 12 V; board E: 34.3 to 15.1 V): 1.0 A 92.0 %; 1.5 A 94.4 %; 2.0 A 95.6 %; 3.0 A 96.0 %; 4.5 A 96.6 %; 6.0 A 96.8 %; 7.5 A 96.7 %; 9.0 A 96.7 %; 10.5 A 96.6 %; 12.0 A 96.5 %; 13.5 A 96.4 %; 14.6 A 96.3 %
   VIN 20 V: 1.0 A 96.3 %; 1.5 A 96.9 %; 2.0 A 97.3 %; 3.0 A 97.7 %; 4.5 A 97.9 %; 6.0 A 97.9 %; 7.5 A 97.8 %; 9.0 A 97.7 %; 10.5 A 97.6 %; 12.0 A 97.4 %; 13.5 A 97.2 %; 14.6 A 97.1 %
   READING at 6 to 12 A on the 35 V curve (board E's stage delivers up to about 12 A at 15.1 V): 96.5 to 96.8 % (INFERRED).
   At light load the curve falls: the 1 to 3 A readings above (the steep part of the curve, where a pixel is worth more).

3. WHAT THE READINGS ARE NOT: a figure for board E or board A, at their voltages, frequencies, inductors, FETs,
   copper or temperature, or weighted over the reference day's hours. They show
   that the makers' own designs run above the energy model's declared 0.93 at the nearest points; they do not
   establish 0.93, or any other figure, for the kit.

END.
